# Dataset

The model is trained on [Solid_State_Electrolyte](https://www.aissquare.com/datasets/detail?name=Solid_State_Electrolyte&id=217&pageType=datasets) dataset. Overall, the training sets encompass 15 elements and 41 distinct systems, including 26 chalcogenides, 14 basic binary compounds, and 1 Li element. The active learning framework (DPGEN) is used to produce the dataset.

# Parameters

The main parameters of training process include a batch size of 1, 1,000,000 steps, and the DPA-2 descriptor with cutoff radii (rcut) and selected numbers of neighbors (nsel) in the repinit layer and the repformer layer are 9.0 Å and 120, 4.0 Å and 40, respectively.

# Performances

||Energy RMSE (eV/atom)|Force RMSE (eV/Å)|
|-|-|-|
|Data std.|1.03E-01|6.67E-01|
|From scratch|3.58E-03|5.32E-02|

# Usage

One can use the following command to test the performance of the model in <test_system>.

```bash
dp --pt test -m SSE-VASP-dpa2.pt -s <test_system>
```


